    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. **Yordan Alvarez** projects as the team\u2019s anchor with a 76.88 score, buoyed by an elite 0.450 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Tanner Bibee. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.81) is a critical play for our stolen base-starved roster; he benefits from a +14% dynamic platoon boost and a matchup against Kevin Gausman, whose slow delivery provides the perfect environment for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to capitalize on his speed. **Colt Keith** also provides significant value, climbing to a 69.64 score thanks to a soft matchup against Erick Fedde, where a wind-aided environment and a favorable batting order position amplify his upside.\n\nStrategic depth remains a focus as we manage our daily efficiency caps. The most difficult decision rested between **Nelson Velazquez** (55.25) and **Casey Schmitt** (41.80). While **Casey Schmitt** offered a solid floor, the optimizer opted for the high-end xwOBA potential of **Nelson Velazquez**, who despite a slight platoon disadvantage, maintains a significantly higher ceiling in run-producing spots. We have largely avoided starting options against the day\u2019s toughest arm, Tarik Skubal, though **Chase Meidroth** (49.98) retains his spot due to the high-leverage leadoff opportunity and helpful wind conditions. \n\nRisk management remains a primary concern as we await official confirmations for **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Colt Keith**, **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, and **Junior Caminero**. Since the majority of our lineup is currently marked \"Lineup Pending,\" any drastic shifts in batting order\u2014specifically moving **Chase Meidroth** or **Christian Yelich** out of the leadoff spot\u2014will force us to re-evaluate our efficiency targets. With **Trea Turner** currently inactive, we are relying on high-volume production from the rest of the squad to maintain our 5x5 pace.",
